From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:09:54 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 83/93] Plutonium: ext_idle_notify_v1, apps hear when the user
 is idle

Discord's and chat apps' away status, and swayidle, need it. Version
2: a notification goes idle after its timeout without a key, pointer or
touch (Ash's UserActivityDetector) and resumes at the next one. Those
made with get_idle_notification are also held off while something
inhibits idle, and count again from when it stopped; the helper's
session service knows every inhibitor (the shells', apps' over D-Bus
and the portal, the browser's wake locks, zwp_idle_inhibit) and says
whether there are any with the new Plutonium.setIdleInhibited, which
goes back to false when its client goes. As in wlroots, an inhibitor
coming while idle leaves the notification idle.
